  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center of Women&apos;s Legal Research</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CWLRCP will expand the Hayat GBV Shelter, the only facility in Gaza dedicated to supporting GBV survivors, to strengthen its capacity and impact. In addition, legal support will be provided to women who have faced challenges such as family disputes, domestic violence, inheritance issues, or discrimination, and who require assistance in pursuing legal action or obtaining official documents&#x2014;including death certificates, inheritance records, custody papers, and ID documents&#x2014;due to the destruction caused by the Israeli war. CWLRCP will also offer personalized, confidential individual sessions for 200 women and girls from the same target group to address specific case management needs. Furthermore, psychosocial support (PSS) services will be delivered to 4,000 women and girls in 10 temporary shelters through group consultations, intervention sessions, awareness-raising activities, and recreational programs, with specialized support available for GBV survivors. To enhance access to multisectoral services, CWLRCP will scale up its offices to establish safe, inclusive, and supportive environments offering legal, psychological, educational, and awareness services for women and girls in Gaza. Additionally, CWLRCP will conduct one-day (5-hour) training sessions on Protection from Sexual Exploitation and Abuse(PSEA) and safe referrals for 200 committee members (60 women and 140 men) at displacement shelters, aiming to reach 250 beneficiaries</narrative>
  </description>
